## POST 73: Siding Replacement Cost: What Homeowners Actually Pay

# Siding Replacement Cost: What Homeowners Actually Pay

**Meta Title:** Average Siding Replacement Cost | Tampa Florida **Meta Description:** Real siding replacement costs by home size and material type. Learn about hidden costs, financing, insurance, and ROI for Tampa homes.

**Primary Keyword:** siding replacement cost (1,900/mo, KD 6) **Secondary Keywords:** cost to replace siding, siding replacement price, new siding cost, home siding replacement, siding installation cost

Replacing your home’s siding is a significant investment, but it’s also one of the most impactful improvements you can make. If you’re considering siding replacement in Tampa, understanding actual costs—not just estimates, but what homeowners really pay—helps you budget accurately and avoid sticker shock.

## Real-World Costs by Home Size

### Small Homes (1,000–1,500 sq ft)

For a typical small Tampa home, expect approximately 2,500–3,500 linear feet of siding.

**Vinyl siding:** $30,000–$56,000 total ($12–$20 per linear foot installed) **Aluminum siding:** $37,500–$70,000 total ($15–$25 per linear foot installed) **Fiber cement:** $50,000–$87,500 total ($20–$30 per linear foot installed)

### Average Homes (1,500–2,500 sq ft)

Most Tampa homes fall into this category, requiring 3,500–5,500 linear feet.

**Vinyl siding:** $42,000–$110,000 total ($12–$20 per linear foot installed) **Aluminum siding:** $52,500–$137,500 total ($15–$25 per linear foot installed) **Fiber cement:** $70,000–$165,000 total ($20–$30 per linear foot installed)

### Large Homes (2,500+ sq ft)

Homes with complex rooflines or significant square footage (5,500+ linear feet) can easily reach $150,000–$300,000+ depending on material choice.

## Material Comparison: What You’ll Actually Pay

**Vinyl Siding:** $12–$20 installed - Most affordable option - Requires minimal maintenance - 20–30 year lifespan in Florida - Popular for value-conscious homeowners

**Aluminum Siding:** $15–$25 installed - Mid-range cost - Excellent durability, especially for Florida - Minimal maintenance - 30–50 year lifespan

**Fiber Cement:** $20–$30 installed - Premium option - Best durability and weather resistance - Can mimic wood appearance - 25–40 year lifespan

**Engineered Wood:** $18–$28 installed - Attractive aesthetic - Requires regular maintenance - Less ideal for Florida’s humidity - 15–25 year lifespan

## Hidden Costs Many Homeowners Don’t Anticipate

### Underlayment and House Wrap

Modern installation requires moisture barrier and house wrap: $2–$6 per linear foot, adding $7,000–$33,000 to total cost.

Proper underlayment is critical in Tampa’s humid climate—don’t skip this to save money.

### Flashing and Trim

Corners, windows, doors, and roof transitions require flashing material and labor. Budget $2,000–$5,000 for complete flashing installation.

Poor flashing is the #1 cause of water intrusion; professional flashing is worth every penny.

### Soffit, Fascia, and Gutters

If your gutters, soffit, or fascia need concurrent replacement, add $5,000–$15,000 depending on home size and material choice.

Many contractors offer bundled pricing when coordinating these installations.

### Permits and Inspections

Florida building codes require permits for siding replacement: $500–$1,500 depending on county (Hillsborough, Pinellas, Pasco, etc.).

Permit costs are non-negotiable and ensure installation meets code.

### Roof Repairs Discovered During Replacement

Removing siding sometimes reveals roof issues or wood rot. Budget $3,000–$10,000 in case repairs are necessary.

### Disposal and Cleanup

Hauling old siding to the dump or recycling: $1,000–$3,000 depending on volume.

## Financing Your Siding Replacement

Many homeowners don’t pay cash for siding replacement. Financing options include:

**Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC):** Typically 3–5% APR, flexible terms **Home Improvement Loans:** Fixed-rate, 3–7 years, 5–8% APR **Contractor Financing:** 0% for 12–24 months, or fixed-rate options **Credit Card Rewards:** For smaller projects or cash-back opportunities

## Insurance Claims for Storm Damage

If your siding damage is from documented storm events (hail, hurricanes, high winds), your homeowner’s insurance may cover 50–100% of replacement costs after your deductible.

**Steps to maximize insurance coverage:** 1. Document damage with photos immediately after the storm 2. File a claim within your policy timeframe (usually 1–3 years) 3. Request a professional inspection report 4. Have an insurance adjuster assess damage 5. Request itemized quotes from contractors

In Tampa, many homeowners have successfully recovered $10,000–$30,000+ through insurance claims for storm damage.

## ROI: Does Siding Replacement Pay Off?

Siding replacement typically recovers 75–85% of its cost at resale in Florida’s competitive market. For a $60,000 investment, expect $45,000–$51,000 in recovered value.

**Additional ROI benefits:** - Lower energy costs (insulted vinyl/fiber cement) - Reduced maintenance expenses - Improved curb appeal (typically 5–10% higher perceived value) - Peace of mind from weather protection

## FAQs About Siding Replacement Cost

**Q: What’s the cheapest siding material?** A: Vinyl siding is the most affordable at $12–$20 per linear foot installed, with an average 2,000 sq ft home costing $30,000–$56,000.

**Q: Does insurance pay for siding replacement?** A: Storm damage is often covered. Wear and tear is not. Documentation and professional assessment are key.

**Q: Can I replace just part of my home’s siding?** A: Yes, but full replacement often looks more cohesive. Partial replacement costs $5,000–$25,000 depending on scope.

**Q: How long does siding replacement take?** A: Average homes take 2–4 weeks. Complex projects may take 4–8 weeks.

## Get an Accurate Quote for Your Home

Siding replacement costs vary significantly based on home size, material choice, underlying damage, and local labor rates. The only way to know what *your* project will cost is through a professional assessment.

**JR One Aluminum** provides free, detailed estimates with no pressure. Our 30+ years of experience means we’ve completed hundreds of siding replacements throughout Tampa and surrounding areas.

**Call (844) 444-3114 today for your free estimate.** We’ll assess your home, explain all costs upfront, and help you understand your financing options and insurance possibilities.

